  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  name: weaviate-client\n  version: \"4.24.1\"\n\npackage:\n  name: ${{ name|lower }}\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  # 4.24.0 and 4.24.1 were published to PyPI as wheels only, so build from the GitHub tag\n  url: https://github.com/weaviate/weaviate-python-client/archive/refs/tags/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 7987b198a838b65f4d3056aac3f2cd7fda3bbbf065998b87e5821ad2a182c1c5\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  noarch: python\n  script:\n    env:\n      # the GitHub tarball has no git metadata for setuptools-scm\n      SETUPTOOLS_SCM_PRETEND_VERSION: ${{ version }}\n    content:\n      # setup.cfg lists only top-level packages and relies on the setuptools-scm\n      # git file finder (include_package_data) to ship subpackages such as\n      # weaviate/proto/v1/v6300; without git metadata, a MANIFEST.in does that job\n      - echo \"graft weaviate\" > MANIFEST.in\n      - ${{ PYTHON }} -m pip install . -vv --no-deps --no-build-isolation\n\nrequirements:\n  host:\n    - python ${{ python_min }}.*\n    - pip\n    - setuptools >=65\n    # setuptools_scm[toml] needs nothing extra on conda-forge\n    - setuptools-scm >6.2\n    - wheel >=0.38.1\n  run:\n    - python >=${{ python_min }}\n    - httpx >=0.26.0,<0.29.0\n    - certifi >=2026.10.19\n    - validators >=0.34.0,<1.0.0\n    - authlib >=1.7.1,<2.0.0\n    - pydantic >=2.12.0,<3.0.0\n    - grpcio >=1.59.5,<1.80.0\n    - protobuf >=4.21.6,<7.0.0\n    - packaging >=21.0\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - weaviate\n      pip_check: true\n      python_version:\n        - ${{ python_min }}.*\n        - \"*\"\n\nabout:\n  summary: A python native Weaviate client\n  license: BSD-3-Clause\n  license_file: LICENSE\n  homepage: https://github.com/weaviate/weaviate-python-client\n  repository: https://github.com/weaviate/weaviate-python-client\n  documentation: https://weaviate.io/developers/weaviate/client-libraries/python\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - xylar\n",
